| compose_keeps_obligation | No disjunct; membership moves from an intermediate residual into the combined trace, not into final pending obligations. The concrete settled-after-resume session makes the distinction real. |
| atomic_locality | Iff, no disjunct; actual finite index and touches predicate characterize the log of judgment work. This is exact rejudgment locality, not a claim that list scanning costs O(touched). |
| resume_coherent | No disjunct; old coherence establishes new-world coherence after an actual edit. |
| choose_sound | No disjunct; returned candidate belongs to retained input and meets both intent and current judge. Both filters have real disabling plants. |
| choose_none | No disjunct; excludes verified eligible candidates only within the supplied list. Does not refute the hole or all possible constructions. |
| select_authorized | No disjunct; policy wrapper success is tied to the separate landed authority/history operation at the returned index. |
| select_sound | No disjunct; I and c are pinned by find and finite index, with authority, unaccepted state, fresh judgment, live supports and resulting sigma. |
| transport_sound | No disjunct; registry law alone does not supply success or the image/dependency facts. Success ties exact certificate and correspondence to input, image, inverse and freshly verified destination, conserving source effective supports. |
| transport_typing | No disjunct; forward checker preservation is connected through complete/sound calculus laws to the actual HasTy judgment. Destination admission is a separate issue. |
| transported_not_replacement | No disjunct; constructor-disjointness representation law only, not proof of equivalence. |
| choose_index | No disjunct; both offset bound and exact indexed candidate are established by recursive search; c cannot be an unrelated optimal witness. |
| choose_minimal | No disjunct; compares against every eligible verified input candidate. Reflexivity handles only the chosen candidate, not cheaper alternatives. |
| conditional_soundness | No disjunct; coherence links recorded verification to current typing, guard, blockers, supports and hard budget. Does not assert whole-template derivability. |
| withTransport_sound | No disjunct; structural state frame law for offers. An unsound registry cannot be used to derive transport_sound from it. |
| select_preference | No disjunct; exact actual selection index/candidate, intent and minimum over all eligible verified alternatives. |
| Experiments.withdraw_resume_session | No disjunct; decide executes propose/select, withdrawal, assertion and composition; exact status and obligation lists, including retained intermediate checkpoint. |
| Experiments.policy_session | No disjunct; decide computes different retained indices under cost versus intent, plus wrong-party and accepted-state rejection. |
| Experiments.preference_cannot_waive_budget | No disjunct; real over-budget proposal retained by session but selection fails even under zero preference cost. |
| Experiments.representation_equivalence | No disjunct; four universal laws for arbitrary Nat payloads with distinct Bool representations. Inverse is not an identity conversion. Data-only fixture is explicitly not a lawful contextual calculus. |
| Experiments.registry_checked | No disjunct; successful lookup at 17 is nonempty and is the proved two-sided correspondence; no empty-registry trick. |
| Experiments.transport_session | No disjunct; six decide computations separately test converted output and unknown-certificate/source-type/destination-guard/support/budget rejection. |
| Experiments.identity_transport_fails | No disjunct; source representation fails target checking and forward image passes, so conversion is operationally necessary. |
| Experiments.transport_in_repair_result | No disjunct; actual wrapper success/refusal metadata is computed. Unselected sigma is a frame/API fact, not equivalence evidence. |
| Experiments.initial_coherent | No disjunct; world and closure are fixed by actual successful nonempty Session.run, and coherence follows preservation. |
| Experiments.transported_filling_selects | No disjunct; transport image is proposed and selected through ordinary Session.run in the explicit new template, yielding the concrete sigma value. |

